<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mansa Musa's pilgrimage</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1324">1324</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mansa-musa">Mansa Musa</a>'s pilgrimage was the journey of the ruler of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mali-empire">Mali Empire</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mecca">Mecca</a> in 1324. Accompanied by a vast retinue, he distributed so much gold, notably in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cairo">Cairo</a>, that its value there is reported to have fallen. The pilgrimage spread <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mali">Mali</a>'s reputation for wealth across the Islamic world and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>.</p></div>
